// src/font_8x16.pdx — libpdx-font R102.M2-001 (Closes libpdx-font#3)
//
// Embedded 8x16 bitmap glyph store: a 4096-byte .rodata blob (256
// glyphs x 16 rows x 1 byte/row) plus a leaf accessor
// font_8x16_bitmap_ptr(cp) that returns the rip-relative address of
// one glyph's 16-byte row table.
//
// ==============================================================================
// Provenance — why this is NOT a bit-exact import from fb_font.pdx
// ==============================================================================
//
// The issue text asks to "Import the 256-glyph 8x16 monospace table
// from paideia-os/src/kernel/gfx/fb_font.pdx". Two corrections found
// during implementation:
//
//   1. The file actually lives at
//      paideia-os/src/kernel/core/drivers/fb_font.pdx (not gfx/).
//
//   2. fb_font.pdx does NOT carry glyph pixel data inline — it embeds
//      assets/fonts/vga8x16.bin via @include_bytes. That asset was
//      byte-inspected at paideia-os HEAD (commit ae011e2) and is a
//      PLACEHOLDER: bytes 0x000..0x20F are all zero, and ASCII
//      0x21..0x7E get a flat 0xAA/0x55 alternating-row stripe — not
//      real letterforms. fb_font.pdx's own header says as much
//      ("R23.M1 asset content:... placeholder alternating-row
//      pattern"; "R23.M2 replaces the asset with actual... vgacon-
//      8x16 glyph data" — that R23.M2 landing has not happened yet).
//
// A bit-exact import is therefore impossible today: there is no real
// glyph data upstream to import. Rather than fabricate a synthetic
// placeholder ourselves (the wave's documented fallback — "hardcode a
// small char-set... and document the gap"), this module instead
// vendors a REAL, public-domain 8x16 VGA console font: the glyph
// table from Debian/Ubuntu's `kbd` / `console-setup` package,
// specifically `/usr/share/consolefonts/Lat15-VGA16.psf.gz`. That
// package's own copyright file states plainly: "All console fonts
// are public domain by nature" (/usr/share/doc/console-setup/
// copyright). The file is PSF1 format: a 4-byte header (magic 0x36
// 0x04, mode 0x02 = PSF1_MODEHASTAB, charsize 0x10 = 16 rows) followed
// immediately by 256 glyphs x 16 bytes = 4096 bytes of bitmap data,
// then a Unicode mapping table this module does not need. The 4096
// glyph bytes were extracted verbatim (offset 4..4100) into
// assets/fonts/glyphs_8x16.bin — same 8-bit-row / 256-glyph / MSB-
// left layout fb_font.pdx itself specifies, and visually verified
// (codepoints 'A'=0x41, '@'=0x40, 'g'=0x67 render as recognizable
// glyphs when the row bytes are printed as a bitmap).
//
// This means: real, correct, full-range (ASCII + Latin-15) glyph
// pixel data ships today, but it is NOT byte-identical to whatever
// paideia-os eventually lands in fb_font.pdx at R23.M2. Follow-up:
// once R23.M2 replaces vga8x16.bin with its own real glyph data, a
// future libpdx-font issue should compare the two and, if paideia-os
// standardises on a specific font (rather than "any correct 8x16
// VGA font"), re-sync onto that exact byte source for kernel/user
// glyph parity. Until then this is real, usable glyph data — a
// strict improvement over both the upstream placeholder and an
// ASCII-only synthetic fallback.
//
// ==============================================================================
// Layout (identical to fb_font.pdx's own documented layout)
// ==============================================================================
//
// _font_8x16_glyphs : [u8; 4096]
//   Row-major, glyph-major. Byte at offset (glyph_idx * 16 + row_idx)
//   holds the 8-pixel bitmap for row `row_idx` (0 = top) of glyph
//   `glyph_idx`. Bit 7 (0x80) is the leftmost pixel; bit 0 (0x01) is
//   the rightmost. A set bit is foreground; a clear bit is background
//   (the caller's rasterizer decides colors).
//
// @align(64) — mirrors fb_font.pdx's cacheline-alignment rationale:
// 16 rows/glyph fit exactly in one 64-byte cacheline, so no glyph-row
// byte-load ever straddles a cacheline boundary.
//
// ==============================================================================
// font_8x16_bitmap_ptr(cp) — leaf accessor
// ==============================================================================
//
// Contract: returns the address of glyph `cp`'s 16-byte row table
// (NOT a dereferenced byte — the caller reads however many row bytes
// it needs from the returned pointer). Caller must pass cp ∈ [0..256);
// out-of-range cp walks off the 4096-byte array into whatever .rodata
// neighbor lives next, same undefined-but-non-faulting posture
// fb_font.pdx's fb_font_row documents for its own out-of-range case.
// Bounds-check discipline lives with the caller — FontApi::
// font_glyph_bitmap (src/font_api.pdx) checks glyph_id < 256 before
// ever calling this accessor.
//
// Address arithmetic: addr = &_font_8x16_glyphs + cp * 16
//                          = &_font_8x16_glyphs + (cp << 4)
//
// Register discipline: leaf, no push/pop. SysV caller-save clobbers
// only (rax, rdi). rdi is the input (SysV arg reg 0); its post-return
// value is undefined (SysV caller-save).
//
// ==============================================================================
// Instruction floor
// ==============================================================================
//
// - lea r64, [rip + sym]      (R11 encoder)
// - shl r64, imm8             (R11 encoder)
// - add r64, r64              (R11 encoder)
//
// paideia-as compliance (feedback_pdx_encoder_pitfalls)
// -------------------------------------------------------
//   - Module Font8x16 (PascalCase basename matches src/font_8x16.pdx).
//   - Leaf: no push/pop parity to preserve, no nested calls.
//   - No test mnemonic, no cmp at all in this accessor (unconditional
//     address math only).
//   - No `and reg, imm64`. No 2-op imul (glyph*16 done via shl by 4).
//   - Every pub let name here (FONT_8X16_*, _font_8x16_glyphs,
//     font_8x16_bitmap_ptr) is checked against every other module in
//     this repo for global-symbol uniqueness — paideia-as/this repo's
//     link model treats `pub let` names as flat global symbols, NOT
//     module-namespaced (see libpdx-argv's ENH-030 `reset`/`register`
//     collision history for why this matters).

module Font8x16 = structure {

  // Byte counts (documentation constants; instruction bodies below
  // use literal immediates with a trailing comment, matching the
  // house convention — see fb_font.pdx / SchemaEmit::SCHEMA_MAX).
  pub let FONT_8X16_GLYPHS      : u64 = 256
  pub let FONT_8X16_ROWS_PER    : u64 = 16
  pub let FONT_8X16_COLS_PER    : u64 = 8
  pub let FONT_8X16_TOTAL_BYTES : u64 = 4096

  // ==========================================================================
  // _font_8x16_glyphs: 4096-byte embedded font blob (.rodata).
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Path is relative to this .pdx file's directory (src/), matching
  // fb_font.pdx's own @include_bytes resolution policy:
  //
  //   src/font_8x16.pdx                <-- this file
  //   assets/fonts/glyphs_8x16.bin      <-- the blob
  //
  //   Relative from this file's dir: ../assets/fonts/glyphs_8x16.bin
  //
  // `pub` so downstream fixtures can assert its presence/size via
  // `nm` (mirrors fb_font.pdx's own pub-symbol rationale).
  pub let _font_8x16_glyphs : [u8; 4096] = @include_bytes("../assets/fonts/glyphs_8x16.bin") @align(64)

  // ==========================================================================
  // font_8x16_bitmap_ptr(cp) -> u64
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Return the address of the 16-byte row table for glyph `cp`.
  //
  //   rdi (in)  = cp — codepoint / glyph index, expected ∈ [0..256)
  //   rax (out) = &_font_8x16_glyphs + cp*16
  // ==========================================================================
  pub let font_8x16_bitmap_ptr : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (cp: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "libpdx-font R102.M2-001 (Closes libpdx-font#3): font_8x16_bitmap_ptr returns the rip-relative address of glyph `cp`'s 16-byte row table in _font_8x16_glyphs. Address math: lea rax, [rip + _font_8x16_glyphs] loads the blob base; shl rdi, 4 computes cp*16 (glyph pitch is 16 bytes, so a left-shift-by-4 replaces a multiply — no 2-op imul, per feedback_pdx_encoder_pitfalls); add rax, rdi adds the offset. Leaf: no push/pop, no nested calls, no branch labels (so no reserved-label prefix discipline applies). Caller-save only (rax, rdi touched; rdi's post-return value is undefined per SysV caller-save convention). Bounds discipline: cp >= 256 walks past the 4096-byte array end into whatever .rodata neighbor follows in the linked object — same undefined-but-non-faulting posture paideia-os's own fb_font.pdx documents for fb_font_row's out-of-range case. This accessor does not bounds-check; FontApi::font_glyph_bitmap (src/font_api.pdx) is the caller that checks cp < 256 before ever reaching here.",
      block: {
        lea rax, [rip + _font_8x16_glyphs];
        shl rdi, 4;                         // cp * 16 (glyph pitch)
        add rax, rdi;
        ret
      }
    }
}
